{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions","id":969102,"title":"Mythological Crossover questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-14T02:30:27-07:00","id":969102,"title":"Mythological Crossover questions","content":"IF you use crossover, how do you resolve the differences in mythology of the different cWoD games?<br /> I do realize that the views of the individual supernatural species when it comes to creation of the world, cosmology, mythology and that kinda stuff can be biased, different interpretations of the same thing and several other things but how do you handle it?<br /> <br /> I talked about that a bit with the guy who has been a storyteller for games I play in for a few years already (and he has been a player and storyteller for much longer already) but he is mainly a Werewolf guy, not really about Crossover so much.<br /> <br /> Personally I have no idea about Mage, Wraith, Mummy, Hunter and so on but have played Werewolf and Vampire quite a bit and am also quite big on Demon: the Fallen even though I doubt I'll get to play it anytime soon (and haven't even read all the material yet).<br /> <br /> My friend told me his main problem with Demon is that its cosmological/mythical background does not fit with the rest at all while for example Werewolf and Vampire can work together quite well. I'm not so sure about that though.<br /> I mean Demon kind of gives an explanation for different points of view (in short on different plains of perception ALL of them are true and the same thing) but fails to include anything about other stuff like large parts of the Umbra. That might be because, if I remember correctly, Fera didn't even exist at the time when the Fallen were banished into the Abyss. That still doesn't explain the connections in the background though.<br /> Vampire and Werewolf don't include anything about the Fallen of course since the game wasn't around when their material was written.<br /> Werewolf, as far as I'm aware totally ignores God/The Creator while in Vampire background its pretty central that God cursed Cain and that is how Vampires came into being (and Demon mentions that the Fallen learned the concept of killing other beings (something totally alien to them beforehand) from that same Cain when he was observed slaying his brother).<br /> Seeing this I actually think that Vampire and Demon would be the easiest to combine while Werewolf seems the total outlier of the three (and I don't know about the rest of the games).<br /> <br /> I guess it comes down to the question of who/what you take God/the Creator to be compared to the top &quot;players&quot; in Fera mythology.<br /> As far as I know different Fera and even different Werewolfs have different opinions if Gaia is a level higher or lower than the Triat (Wyld, Weaver, Wyrm). Then what would God equal in their background? Gaia? the Wyld maybe as that's the principle of creation (though much more chaotic than God appears in Vampire and Demon)?<br /> <br /> Any important pieces of info I'm missing? Any insights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T03:44:21-07:00","id":969124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions#post969102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF you use crossover, how do you resolve the differences in mythology of the different cWoD games?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's...hard. Putting all the gamelines side-by-side equally, things do not mesh well, and directly contradict at times.<br /> <br /> As all the origin stories and world mythologies are conflicting more or less, the only way to really resolve it is to decide on <i>one gameline</i> that you label as '<i>Correct</i>' for your game, and then take the other gameline's explanations and make them work in that context.<br /> <br /> Demon *<i>tried</i>* this of course, by being the one gameline that says '<i>All the others are wrong, this is how things really are</i>', but in turnabout it was completely biased on the Demons.<br /> Which is fine. It essentially did what an ST has to do for crossovers without ending up with a mess, so it already served that option in the book. But it basically simply is the '<i>Demon is correct</i>' option.<br /> <br /> So, basically,<br /> 1) Decide on true gameline origin story for your game<br /> 2) Weave the others in in that dominant context.<br /> <br /> The characters of course can believe whatever they want.<br /> <br /> Vampire and Demon indeed are the easiest to combine. Mage can *explain* everything, but does so in a grand 'reality is what humanity makes of it' manner, which can strongly take away the significance of the other mythologies. Werewolf brings the whole Gaia/Triad origin story with it and forces everything else to quite bend and warp in order to fit and somewhat make sense.<br /> <br /> Pick your poison <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Or, you know, if it simply plays no role in the plots you run, just ignore it all as long as it doesn't come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-14-2016, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:32:44-07:00","id":969274,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is the nature of God. The God of Abrahamic religions did not really exist until after the Babylonian Exile, when the Jews, influenced by the exposure to Zorastrian ideology, rejected their Pantheon to create a two diety religion. YHWH became the 'good' god while Lucifer became the 'bad' god. Instead of having two equal gods, however, the Jews made to 'good' god superior to the 'bad god, which has led to over 2500 years of argument of why the 'good' god lets the 'bad' god do bad things. Presumably, the eldest vampires remember the change and the Mokole can access Mnesis to remember the change.<br /> <br /> Werewolf possesses the broadest, the oldest, and the most internally logical mythology (though individual groups have their distortions and their biases). Even so, there is no evidence that any of the Changing Breeds have left the Solar System, so their mythologies are decidedly local. I like to think that Gaia is merely the local manifestation of the Universe while the Triat are local manifestations of the corresponding universal principles. Further, I like to think that the Solar System is experiencing a quarantine from the outside to prevent the corruption of its local manifestations from spreading. Just my two cents...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:52:51-07:00","id":969287,"title":"","content":"Aya Tari, please, be careful, you are talking about a real religi\u00f3n. I don't believe Hindu pantheon but I can't talk in public about them like simple myths. And do remember Yaveh isn't like a invisible friend, because He said a lot of things people of Israel didn't want to hear. Most of prophets weren't respected by people from their generation and Judaism is monotheist, not monolatry or henoteism, and that is very important.<br /> <br /> * Other theory is the WoD demons aren't really the true and original from Hell but &quot;broken shards of something&quot; when they fallen to Earth become like close to main religions, I mean the true origin of Wod demons would be like Asgardians from the marvel comic saga &quot;Earth X&quot;, a alien group when they arrived to Earth they become Viking myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T10:41:11-07:00","id":969310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969274#post969274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf possesses the broadest, the oldest, and the most internally logical mythology (though individual groups have their distortions and their biases). Even so, there is no evidence that any of the Changing Breeds have left the Solar System, so their mythologies are decidedly local.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of Garou and Fera have gone questing through the Aetherial Realm through the ages; there's an entire society known as th Wagnerians that does this, and the vast majority of Nuwisha are off in the depths of various umbral frontiers all the time. Corax are also very well traveled, particularly the Sun-Lost. Revised also gave the answer that there is no relief force from another planet's spirit world, and you cannot count on any cavalry to bail you out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like to think that Gaia is merely the local manifestation of the Universe while the Triat are local manifestations of the corresponding universal principles. Further, I like to think that the Solar System is experiencing a quarantine from the outside to prevent the corruption of its local manifestations from spreading. Just my two cents... </div> </div> </div>That's not really a way in which the relevant spirit world functions. The captivity of the Wyrm happened in the Deep Umbra, and not a definite physical location; it has echoes that are universal and transcend physical distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:32:25-07:00","id":969335,"title":"","content":"As for the first point, that is true, but the Aetherial Realm does not extend beyond the Outer Sol System (and I never suggested that there was anyone from outside that would rescue the Earth). As for the second point, the Deep Umbra of the Garou is the High Umbra of Mage (the Deep Umbra of Mage is Outer Space for the Garou), so the Wyrm is trapped within the Deep Umbra of the Garou or the High Umbra of Mage. <br /> <br /> I think that the quarantine of the Sol System would be a logical explanation for the lack of visitors from alien civilizations. If every neighboring alien civilization understands that there is a horrific spiritual contagion located in the Sol System, they would probably want to stay away. They would also probably have a patrol which would maintain the quarantine and destroy anything that would attempts to breech the quarantine. Just a thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:35:00-07:00","id":969384,"title":"","content":"My take on things is this:<br /> <br /> <i>Every</i> story is, or was, true. When Chaos, Order and Entropy war one upon the other, time and history become weapons. The tiny things on Earth only perceive the barest hint of the Outer Darkness waging war on the light. This is for the best: seeing too much of the conflict's true scope would annihilate the sanity of even the strongest non-divine being.<br /> <br /> Entropy destroys; so Chaos creates anew. Order tries to halt the process entirely. Every time this iteration plays itself out, changes to space/time inevitably occur: the past is mutable. It <i>changes</i>.<br /> <br /> But Entropy is slowly winning, and so, rather than fade away, the shells of previous worlds collide with ours, leaving imprints of truths no longer valid in the current timeline. As the wheel of ages grinds to a final close, the past burns and now clear history is impossible to discern.<br /> <br /> It's <i>all</i> true, even if it no longer <i>true</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:49:02-07:00","id":969395,"title":"","content":"As for aliens:<br /> <br /> As the oWoD is a horror setting, if aliens exists, then they are <i>different</i> to the point of incomprehensibility. Ascribing human emotions and human motivations to such things is, at best, unwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:23:21-07:00","id":969449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969274#post969274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of having two equal gods, however, the Jews made to 'good' god superior to the 'bad god, which has led to over 2500 years of argument of why the 'good' god lets the 'bad' god do bad things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire's point of view is that the good creator (Yahweh) is the origin of the soul and spiritual existence. The evil god (Demon Jaldabaoth) created the material world as a prison for the human souls.<br /> <br /> So, the soul is good but the body is corrupt. Humans can seek to ascend by denying their bodies (and the material world) and join the good god.<br /> Vampires, as Jaldabaoth's Jailors, prevent humanity from ascending by corrupting them and forcing them in an unending cycle of death and reincarnation.<br /> <br /> That split caused Jaldabaoth worshipers to support the Albigensian Crusade, and blah blah blah...<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: In <i>State of Grace</i>, there are two vampiric cults that adhere to Werewolf cosmology (Gaians and Primordians).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-14-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:12:28-07:00","id":969511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969335#post969335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the first point, that is true, but the Aetherial Realm does not extend beyond the Outer Sol System</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that both W20 Velvet Shadow and Rage Across the Heavens mention being able to reach more distant stars in the Aetherial, this is incorrect. That's a reference in the portion detailing The Reaches in either book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (and I never suggested that there was anyone from outside that would rescue the Earth). </div> </div> </div>I only mentioned that as the conclusion of the seekers during the Apocalypse, to note that they had searched in the Umbra beyond the Solar System. Apologies if it came across as pointing fingers, that was not my intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the second point, the Deep Umbra of the Garou is the High Umbra of Mage (the Deep Umbra of Mage is Outer Space for the Garou), so the Wyrm is trapped within the Deep Umbra of the Garou or the High Umbra of Mage. </div> </div> </div>Not as of W20, and Malfeas never really played by the rules in earlier editions, either, since it's always been like a Near Realm, but not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that the quarantine of the Sol System would be a logical explanation for the lack of visitors from alien civilizations. If every neighboring alien civilization understands that there is a horrific spiritual contagion located in the Sol System, they would probably want to stay away. They would also probably have a patrol which would maintain the quarantine and destroy anything that would attempts to breech the quarantine. Just a thought... </div> </div> </div>Or it could be that space aliens include beings like the Vhujunka, and that other places didn't fare so well in keeping corruption at bay. This would be somewhat in tune with the time-coordinate version of this assumption from Shattered Dreams, where the past, however crappy, could only be worse. This is how time travel keeps from cluttering up the focus of Werewolf, and taking a similar tack with the space travel similarly maintains focus that keeps the WoD from being outright scifi, unless we're talking the kind of scifi where aliens did arrive on Earth, many times, but they're like flying polyps and not grays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T18:54:22-07:00","id":969593,"title":"","content":"Everyone is wrong. They are all blind men trying to describe an elephant based on what they touch. That things seem to work via two or more contradictory basis is demonstration of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:52:56-07:00","id":969654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969124#post969124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's...hard. Putting all the gamelines side-by-side equally, things do not mesh well, and directly contradict at times.<br /> <br /> As all the origin stories and world mythologies are conflicting more or less, the only way to really resolve it is to decide on <i>one gameline</i> that you label as '<i>Correct</i>' for your game, and then take the other gameline's explanations and make them work in that context.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, basically,<br /> 1) Decide on true gameline origin story for your game<br /> 2) Weave the others in in that dominant context.<br /> <br /> <u>The characters of course can believe whatever they want.</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <u>Or, you know, if it simply plays no role in the plots you run, just ignore it all as long as it doesn't come up.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>These 3 points, with particular emphasis (mine) on the underlined bits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:52:42-07:00","id":969681,"title":"","content":"Or you could go with my idea: They are all right in their respective mythology. Cain is the sire of vampires, Gaia does exist, and Demons did come from the Creator. <br /> <br /> Its like real religion. Just cause I am Christian, doesn't mean Buddhaism is wrong. And vice versa. Gaia existing doesn't matter to Vampires, and Cain being the original Vampire doesn't matter to a Garou. With that thought, each Mythology is right, even in a crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 09-15-2016, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:23:04-07:00","id":969749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969681#post969681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could go with my idea: They are all right in their respective mythology. Cain is the sire of vampires, Gaia does exist, and Demons did come from the Creator.<br /> <br /> Its like real religion. Just cause I am Christian, doesn't mean Buddhaism is wrong. And vice versa. Gaia existing doesn't matter to Vampires, and Cain being the original Vampire doesn't matter to a Garou. With that thought, each Mythology is right, even in a crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I *wish* it could properly be done this way (It would be awesome and save on so many headaches), you run into a problem you don't get with contradicting religions: Each of the cosmologies in the respective gamelines is, mostly, treated as what actually happened. And if you try to do a neutral crossover, you suddenly get a mess.<br /> <br /> Who created the world: Gaia or God?<br /> Are Vampires under God's punishment, or are they actually Wyrm creatures?<br /> If the Wyrm is trying to destroy the world, why isn't God smacking it with a 'Leave my creation alone?'. Or is it actually Gaia's creation, and God is just a bystander to the whole creation shebang? Wait, how does any of it make sense if the Mage's view of 'Reality is shaped by human belief' is true? Or are the Mages wrong? But how can they be wrong, if their whole fight and history is about forcing belief into reality? Did God make the Fae? and how come the Triad decided to let Asia have its whole own 1000 hells? Or did those get created because the Mages are right, and the beliefs of Humans created them all? AAAAAAAAAAA-<br /> <br /> You *can*, with effort, ducttape-and-glue something together that somewhat somehow makes sense out of all these things - but you can't taking each lore fully as-written as a whole and just put them together. :|","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:52:28-07:00","id":969767,"title":"","content":"It's not that hard to come up with solutions for Demon/Werewolf/Vampire. Gaia is God [which Days of Fire does actually seem to hew in the direction of, at least on a vague thematic level], God created Gaia and the Triat and then died/left, or that &quot;God&quot; as comprehended by Demons was the entire system of the Triat and Gaia perceived as a harmonious whole, the engine of Creation that Demons once knew as their master but which has since so fractured and decomposed (alongside the concomitant splitting of the world into Umbra and material reality) as to be unrecognizable. The Demon ST guide even proposes a tenuous link between the Changing Breeds/Garou and the Malhilm warrior-angels manufactured to wipe out the Fallen during the end of the War in Heaven. Things do get kinda screwed up when you try to figure out how many years ago exactly things were supposed to have happened, mind you.<br /> <br /> Demon, Vampire, Hunter, and Wraith are pretty trivially compatible with one another, generally speaking. Werewolf can be tacked on as above (you mostly have to go with Werewolves labeling Oblivion's touch or aberration against nature as 'Wyrm', rather than everything sort of bad being literally a spawn of the Wyrm- i.e. 'Sense Wyrm' does more than just sense Wyrm, but that's what Garou know it as and they will correspondingly label other things in accord with that understanding). Changeling is awkward; DA Fae might fit a little better if you use them for your changelings, although you pretty much need to have the Fae be either some degenerated/mutated permutation of angel or just delusional cogs in the machine of Creation in terms of their history. <br /> <br /> <br /> The exception is Mage. Essentially nothing is particularly compatible with consensual reality in a way that doesn't trivialize everyone else's narrative. You pretty much have to throw most of it out (conceptually and metaphysically Mage never really felt like it fit very well with Wraith/Werewolf/Vampire and later Demon- fighting in space ships in the Umbra and consensual reality and magitek power armor really just could not be further away thematically from the other gamelines).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 09-15-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:54:15-07:00","id":969768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969749#post969749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I *wish* it could properly be done this way (It would be awesome and save on so many headaches), you run into a problem you don't get with contradicting religions: Each of the cosmologies in the respective gamelines is, mostly, treated as what actually happened. And if you try to do a neutral crossover, you suddenly get a mess.<br /> <br /> Who created the world: Gaia or God?<br /> Are Vampires under God's punishment, or are they actually Wyrm creatures?<br /> If the Wyrm is trying to destroy the world, why isn't God smacking it with a 'Leave my creation alone?'. Or is it actually Gaia's creation, and God is just a bystander to the whole creation shebang? Wait, how does any of it make sense if the Mage's view of 'Reality is shaped by human belief' is true? Or are the Mages wrong? But how can they be wrong, if their whole fight and history is about forcing belief into reality? Did God make the Fae? and how come the Triad decided to let Asia have its whole own 1000 hells? Or did those get created because the Mages are right, and the beliefs of Humans created them all? AAAAAAAAAAA-<br /> <br /> You *can*, with effort, ducttape-and-glue something together that somewhat somehow makes sense out of all these things - but you can't taking each lore fully as-written as a whole and just put them together. :|</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It all can actually make sense if you word it right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who created the world: Gaia or God? </div> </div> </div>God. Gaia is Celestial, just like Helios and Luna. In fact, I recall there's even one of the BSD endings to W:tA games where Wyrm has won and BSD actually literally find her, and.. well, bad things happen, including rape and murder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Vampires under God's punishment, or are they actually Wyrm creatures? </div> </div> </div>Under God's punishment. And /as result/ of that, once the &quot;death&quot; of vampires has come, Wyrm the Unmaker has swallowed them - but he discovered that unlike every living thing, they did not die, instead biting the Wyrm right in the gut. Screaming in pain, the Wyrm spat them out, unable to bring their final hour. (It is actually explanation from the books, but I do not remember pages for direct quotes. Though, I can ask my friend who actually has them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Wyrm is trying to destroy the world, why isn't God smacking it with a 'Leave my creation alone?' </div> </div> </div>Because God abandoned Creation and humanity. That's pretty much it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is it actually Gaia's creation, and God is just a bystander to the whole creation shebang? </div> </div> </div>God created it, Gaia is &quot;only&quot; a Celestial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, how does any of it make sense if the Mage's view of 'Reality is shaped by human belief' is true? Or are the Mages wrong? But how can they be wrong, if their whole fight and history is about forcing belief into reality? </div> </div> </div>*Prepares his mage pants*<br /> <br /> Each human soul is quite literally a reflection of God's soul, as described in the Demon book (Demons and Mages have quite a connection in their lores if you read it right). When it is said that God created humans to be similar to their Creator, it is not implied they're similar in their flesh or strength - it is all about soul, and that's why Demons cannot enslave mortals that easily, and only Earthbound can (which is twisted version of Demon, and not the original Lores). The only exception is becoming a Thrall, to which mortal has to willingly agree.<br /> <br /> But back to original question.<br /> <br /> You see, each human soul represents a God, quite literally. Awakening is said to be &quot;waking up the inner god&quot; for a reason. Humans passively shape reality around them, Awakened or not, and that's why phrase &quot;You Will and You Do&quot; (- from M20) fits this so much.<br /> <br /> Mages are not wrong. Reality is indeed shaped by belief, because each human souls is very similar to God's, as Creator made it like that on purpose. (And that's why Spheres can do anything, given enough Arete and ranks. They represent the Creation itself. Just think about it, potentially you can create a whole new universe with power of Spheres if you had enough time and power, and isn't that what God did?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did God make the Fae? and how come the Triad decided to let Asia have its whole own 1000 hells? Or did those get created because the Mages are right, and the beliefs of Humans created them all? </div> </div> </div>Now, I admit, I don't really know Fae lore, but I'm sure there's some explanation to them just like Garou have. God created fundament of Creation, and why is it that Gaia spawned Garou, others could not do something similar? I'm sure there's something or someone to create Fae, if only I had time to read that book.<br /> <br /> As for hells, there are countless of Realms existing out there, and many are holding on just because humans believe in that. Why not let it? And could they stop it even? Or did they care?<br /> <br /> It all can make sense if you actually look at it under right angle. I was sceptical about this as well, but realised that lores are tied much closer than you might think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T02:12:49-07:00","id":969772,"title":"","content":"I only run Mage anyways, so everything is just a different manifestation of the Mage cosmology in my games.<br /> <br /> But if I were to actually do <i>other games than mage</i> (shudder), then I'd carefully tailor everything to fit that game specifically.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b>:<br /> <br /> Vampires are feeding mouths of the Wyrm, step by step eating the world slowly, tearing it's life essence into the gullet of the Wyrm through thousand, metaphorical lamprey-mouths. They function mechanically like dead people possessed by Banes, build them like Formori with a bunch of Spirit Charms themed after being vampires and possessing a hunger like fire.<br /> <br /> Mages are mortals who have pledged themselves entirely to the worldview of a single Celestine, such as Weaver-Mages that work their magic through technology and order or Wyld-Mages that work their magic through life and creativity. They are pledged to a very little aspect of a Celestine and generally work for more important people such as Black Spiral Dancers, the Glass Walkers likewise have a few business mages. There is no Technocratic Union or Council of Nine Mystic Traditions, only a bunch of mortal magic-users with Spirit Charms.<br /> <br /> Wraith and Orpheus are perfect as written.<br /> <br /> I don't use Changeling or Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:53:39-07:00","id":969871,"title":"","content":"So the last few responses (to me at least) say that Crossovers work fine in terms of cosmology. You just have to pervert or throw out entirely a few of the game lines.<br /> That is the games not working with each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:19:02-07:00","id":969974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969749#post969749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Who created the world: Gaia or God?</div> </div> </div> </div>The creation of the universe is so beyond human understanding this question is meaningless. Ask again when you achieve Ascension.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Vampires under God's punishment, or are they actually Wyrm creatures? </div> </div> </div>Both. The spirit world is as much reactive as it is causal. The Wyrm wasn't the source of Toxic waste but it sure as hell is of the wyrm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Wyrm is trying to destroy the world, why isn't God smacking it with a 'Leave my creation alone?'. </div> </div> </div>God works in mysterious ways. Free Will. The Souls of Man Kind are a baby God. All of the Above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or is it actually Gaia's creation, and God is just a bystander to the whole creation shebang? </div> </div> </div>Perhaps God is the High Umbra representaton of the concept while Gaia is the Middle umbral both are reflections of the true creator as seen through our limited understanding of the universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, how does any of it make sense if the Mage's view of 'Reality is shaped by human belief' is true? Or are the Mages wrong? But how can they be wrong, if their whole fight and history is about forcing belief into reality? </div> </div> </div>That clay can be shaped doesn't mean it lacks existence in and of itself. That reality can be shaped by humans is pretty damn universal across the lines(Humans make ALL sorts of spirits, the Dreaming etc) just how much they are really shaping everything is the question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did God make the Fae? </div> </div> </div>Only the 3rd who are angels who didn't take sides.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and how come the Triad decided to let Asia have its whole own 1000 hells? </div> </div> </div>That was determined by the Jade Emperor. Who may be yet another reflection of the One Above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or did those get created because the Mages are right, and the beliefs of Humans created them all? </div> </div> </div>Yes and No. Even ignoring mage Humans make spirits. Humans make spirit realms. Humans make Chimera, Humans Make the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You *can*, with effort, ducttape-and-glue something together that somewhat somehow makes sense out of all these things - but you can't taking each lore fully as-written as a whole and just put them together. :| </div> </div> </div>Or you drop the conceit that the lore is even self consistent within each line. Mage has Cosmological Constants so maybe its not pure &quot;Belief&quot;. Werewolf has all sorts of wierd shit that doesn't quite fit, Vampire has some strong evidence that Caine is entirely made up and 3rd gens are where things really start. You've already decided to throw out a lot of stuff to make lines consistant within themselves, when they aren't intended to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lets look at Demon the Fallen Demons. They are transcendent cosmic beings stuffed into our limited meat bodies and brains. By becoming more human they are redeemed but also are no longer capable of thinking in transcendent fashion but are in fact warped by human belief and cultural visions. They tell a story even they know cannot be true because their brains can no longer properly grok the truth. So things look off, inconsistant and confusing.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll say again the contradictions of the setting are seeing things from a limited perspective or meant to cover this, the &quot;truth&quot; is so complex it breaks down into constant contradictions. Or at least this is my take on pure fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:01:09-07:00","id":970128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969974#post969974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humans Make the Dark Umbra.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Neverborn would probably do something in line with disagreeing with that, for all that they can be understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:47:18-07:00","id":970178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=970128#post970128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Neverborn would probably do something in line with disagreeing with that, for all that they can be understood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Neverborn don't make the various Dark Kingdoms, Relics, Buildings, etc. They may though be responsibile for there being a place for ghosts to go. Or they might just happen to have been built on top of. Even Wraith doesn't really try to answer this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:06:52-07:00","id":972755,"title":"","content":"Orpheus offers the possibility that the Neverborn, contrary to their name, were birthed or parasitically laid into the Labyrinth/proto-Underworld by the ghost of a dead universe that somehow happened upon the one of the setting ages ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:14:02-07:00","id":973166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=969274#post969274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is the nature of God. The God of Abrahamic religions did not really exist until after the Babylonian Exile, when the Jews, influenced by the exposure to Zorastrian ideology, rejected their Pantheon to create a two diety religion. YHWH became the 'good' god while Lucifer became the 'bad' god. Instead of having two equal gods, however, the Jews made to 'good' god superior to the 'bad god, which has led to over 2500 years of argument of why the 'good' god lets the 'bad' god do bad things. Presumably, the eldest vampires remember the change and the Mokole can access Mnesis to remember the change.<br /> <br /> Werewolf possesses the broadest, the oldest, and the most internally logical mythology (though individual groups have their distortions and their biases). Even so, there is no evidence that any of the Changing Breeds have left the Solar System, so their mythologies are decidedly local. I like to think that Gaia is merely the local manifestation of the Universe while the Triat are local manifestations of the corresponding universal principles. Further, I like to think that the Solar System is experiencing a quarantine from the outside to prevent the corruption of its local manifestations from spreading. Just my two cents...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, but not quite. The ancient Israelites never worshiped a &quot;pantheon&quot; and were never polytheistic in the way we would use the term now. What you're referring to is a monolatrous or henotheistic religion, in which the deities of other groups they interacted with were acknowledged as being real, but their god was better and cooler than the others and the only one they actually worshiped. This changes during the Babylonian exile, partly due to Zoroastrian influence as you mention but that is often greatly overstated. The conversation that takes place during this time in Judaism centers on the question of how they could have come to this calamity if they enjoyed God's protection and the gods of other nations were inferior, the theological result of which was the idea that other gods were <i>not</i> real and God was capable of acting through other nations to punish his chosen people for failing in their faith. The concept of &quot;the adversary&quot; does also begin to take shape during this time, but it bears little resemblance to either the Zoroastrian Angra Mainyu or the Christian Devil. The Devil is actually way more complicated theologically and honestly doesn't form into anything we would recognize until the advent of Christianity many centuries later. <br /> <br /> The problem with Werewolf's mythology is that is incredibly contemporary. It comes directly from a late twentieth century culture marinating in post-modernism, neo-shamanism, romantische naturphilosophie, Western reinterpretations of Eastern and indigenous religions, and an assortment of reactions to modern scientific thought. It works great as a fantasy setting, but it doesn't really function as any sort of believable mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:26:55-07:00","id":973350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=973166#post973166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It works great as a fantasy setting, but it doesn't really function as any sort of believable mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that's rather an issue for all the games. They weren't built by Anthropologists/biblical scholars etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:55:45-07:00","id":973495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/969102-mythological-crossover-questions?p=973166#post973166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Werewolf's mythology is that is incredibly contemporary. It comes directly from a late twentieth century culture marinating in post-modernism, neo-shamanism, romantische naturphilosophie, Western reinterpretations of Eastern and indigenous religions, and an assortment of reactions to modern scientific thought. It works great as a fantasy setting, but it doesn't really function as any sort of believable mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that Werewolf had much to do with postmodernism. Yanking the reader up by the collar and asking them in an outraged tone &quot;What the fuck is going on? How did you let it come to this?&quot;, yes, but not so much of &quot;there's no real absolute truth&quot;, because there was an absolute truth that Werewolf has in mind. It's &quot;what's going on is wrong&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:41:02-07:00","id":973562,"title":"","content":"Their really is no problem with the mythology as is. WOD was written so that it isn't even internally consistent in game-lines and many books were written to intentionally sound like propaganda by the factions they spoke about. You can simply leave all the contradictions as is, and in doing so make the story a lot more complex and interesting. The storyteller doesn't need to have a &quot;One True Right Answer&quot; for every story, leaving the mystery can make things far more engaging by leaving interpretation to the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}